=== SURFACE SUMMARY ===
  Native Apple-idiomatic SwiftUI parity of the smart-charge schedule suggestion card.
  The web source is an `AIFeatureCard` wrapped in
  `withAiFeature('smart-charge-schedule-suggestion', …)` and driven by `useAiStream`;
  the native surface reproduces that composition, its data, its states, and its i18n.

  Data sources (web hooks → P1/S8 source seam; no direct HTTP from the view):
    • useTranslation → AIScheduleDraftStrings facade (P1/S10).
    • useAiStream    → AIScheduleDraftSource seam (start/stop/refresh + draft()=stream.start,
                       cancel()=stream.cancel; cancel fires on disappear, mirroring the web
                       AbortController-on-unmount). The view binds AIScheduleDraftModel only.

  Shared components used (web → native counterpart):
    • @/components/ai/AIFeatureCard  → AIScheduleDraftCard (header is hoisted to the surface
      chrome with the freshness envelope; action + output panel reproduced 1:1).
    • @/components/ai/withAiFeature  → the AI-enabled gate: AIScheduleDraftModel.isPresented;
      when off the surface renders nothing (faithful web `return null`), unit-pinned.
    • Composed: AiOutputPanel → AIScheduleOutputPanel (renders nothing pre-run; error row /
      thinking indicator / accumulated draft text), AIThinkingIndicator → AIScheduleThinking
      Indicator (labelled status row + 3 shimmering skeleton lines), AIThinkingDots →
      AIScheduleThinkingDots (in-button), AIBadge → AIScheduleHelixBadge.

  Verbatim web logic ported + unit-pinned (the `useMemo` body + guards):
    body defaults = target_soc 80 · current_soc 20 · max_amps 32 · battery_capacity_kwh 75 ·
      charger_voltage 240 · prefer_off_peak true ; snake_case wire keys; vehicle_id via
      numericVehicleId = `Number(vehicleId) || 0`; depart_by = ISO-8601 UTC (empty/unparseable
      → now, valid instant re-emitted) ; canStart = `!!vehicleId && !!ratePlanId`
      (string-truthy, so "0" is truthy) ; route = "/ai/charging/schedule/draft" (bare — the
      client adds /api/v1, no double prefix).
  States (all render, never a blank box): loading(skeleton) · empty(web `!canStart` — visible
    card with disabled "Ask Helix" + input hint) · error(whole-surface QueryError peer +retry) ·
    ready(the firing card; stream idle/streaming/done/error drives button label + output panel) ·
    stale(chip + one auto-refresh) · offline(cached + chip) · gated-off(web `null`, the only
    intentionally-absent branch, unit-pinned). Stream error renders INLINE in the output panel
    (card stays ready), faithful to AiOutputPanel — distinct from the leaf load-error.
  i18n: the source keys (chargePlanner.aiAgent.title/description/generateButton/badge) + the
    shared Helix/AIFeatureCard/AiOutputPanel keys (helix.askHelix/thinking/badge/tooltip/
    ariaLabel/errorLabel, ai.common.errorUnknown) + native chrome (aiSchedule.*) all resolve
    via the P1/S10 facade; the catalog carries the verbatim web English. No literals in code.
  a11y: card is an accessibility container with a spoken summary (title+description, +draft or
    +error once output exists, via the testable AIScheduleDraftAccessibility seam); the action
    keeps the web aria-label contract "Ask Helix · Draft a schedule"; freshness chip / refresh /
    output / retry all labelled; Dynamic Type via Font.TS; reduce-motion-safe dots & shimmer.
  Telemetry: emits view.opened with surface slug "AISmartChargeScheduleSuggestion" once
    (P1/S11), asserted in the model tests.

